#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:5
msgid "Build"
msgstr "自制"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:7
msgid ""
"**Build** is what is made, in the order it is made in. Where :doc:`Build vs "
"Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>` is the decision, this is "
"the plan that follows from it: a list of steps, and for the one selected, "
"its page of the instructions -- how to make a part, or how to add a link to "
"the assembly."
msgstr ""
"**Build** 讲的是哪些东西是自制的，并按它们被制造的顺序排列。:doc:`Build vs Buy "
"</digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>` "
"是那项决定，而这里是由它导出的计划：一张步骤清单，以及对所选中的那一步，它那一页说明 -- 怎么做一个零件，或者怎么把一条链接装到装配体上。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:14
msgid "In the UI"
msgstr "在界面中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:16
msgid ""
"The order is the order of making: a part's **stock** first and the part "
"itself last; an assembly's links in the order the ASSY file gives them, with"
" each built part preceded by the step that makes it, and -- with "
"**Recursively** -- each built sub-assembly before the step that adds it."
msgstr ""
"这个顺序就是制造的顺序：零件的 **坯料** 在最前，零件本身在最后；装配体的各条链接按 ASSY "
"文件给出的顺序排列，而每一个自制零件之前都插着制造它的那一步，再加上 -- 在 **Recursively** 之下 -- "
"每一个自制子装配体都排在添加它的那一步之前。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:21
msgid ""
"Selecting a step shows its page: the manufacturing instructions for a part, "
"with its **route** drawn where the part declares one, or the step that joins"
" a link to what is already there."
msgstr ""
"选中某一步会显示它那一页：对零件来说是它的制造说明，并在该零件声明了 **加工路径** 时把路径画出来；对链接来说则是把它接到已有部分上的那一步。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:25
msgid ""
"The Manufacturing group's Build tab: the order to make it in, with the "
"selected step's page"
msgstr "Manufacturing 组的 Build 标签页：制造它的顺序，以及所选步骤的那一页"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:30
msgid ""
"The steps and their order are the very ones ``pc instructions`` writes, so a"
" step selected here and a page of that file are the same step."
msgstr "这些步骤及其顺序，正是 ``pc instructions`` 所写出的那些，所以在这里选中的某一步，与那个文件里的某一页是同一步。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:34
msgid "On the command line"
msgstr "在命令行中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:46
msgid "Machine routes: ``pc cam``"
msgstr "机床加工路径：``pc cam``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:48
msgid ""
"An object can say what is cut out of it and how, and ``pc cam`` writes the "
"program a machine does it with. The job lives on the object, in its "
"``manufacturing:`` section, because it is a property of the object rather "
"than of whoever cuts it -- a panel is 18 mm thick and has to be cut through "
"whichever router is asked:"
msgstr ""
"对象可以说明要从它身上切掉什么、以及怎么切，而 ``pc cam`` 会写出机床据以执行的程序。这项加工任务写在对象上，放在它的 "
"``manufacturing:`` 小节里，因为它是对象的属性，而不是加工者的属性——面板厚 18 mm，无论问哪台雕刻机都得把它切穿："

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:72
msgid ""
"Saying something about being cut is the object's **opt-in**, and the whole "
"of it. ``pc cam`` with nothing named produces a route for every sketch and "
"part of the package that declares one and passes over every object that does"
" not, silently -- most objects are never cut, and a package where three "
"parts of forty are is the ordinary case rather than thirty-seven warnings. "
"Naming an object that declares nothing is an error, because naming one is "
"asking about it."
msgstr ""
"只要说了关于切削的事，就算是对象的 **选择加入** ，而且仅此而已。不指定任何名称运行 ``pc cam`` "
"，会为包中每一个声明了该小节的草图和零件生成刀路，并静默跳过所有没有声明的对象——大多数对象从来不需要切削，四十个零件里有三个要切的包是常态，而不是三十七条警告。指名一个什么都没声明的对象则是错误，因为指名它就是在问它。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:79
msgid ""
"Unlike a solver, PartCAD **ships an implementation**: ``//builtin/cam`` "
"writes G-code, and ``camImplementation`` names it by default. A route is "
"arithmetic on the object's own outline rather than somebody else's program "
"with a release cycle of its own, which is the test ``export:`` and "
"``render:`` already pass and ``cae:`` does not -- so it ships here for the "
"same reason DXF does. A controller that wants a dialect of its own is a "
"package declaring a file type in its own ``cam:`` section (see :ref:`cam-"
"section`), named by that option, by the object's own ``implementation:``, or"
" by ``-i`` for one run."
msgstr ""
"与求解器不同，PartCAD **自带一个实现** ： ``//builtin/cam`` 会写出 G 代码，而 "
"``camImplementation`` 默认就指向它。刀路是在对象自身轮廓上做的算术，而不是别人那套有自己发布周期的程序——这正是 "
"``export:`` 和 ``render:`` 已经通过、而 ``cae:`` 没有通过的那项检验，所以它随 PartCAD 一起提供，理由和 "
"DXF 一样。想要自有方言的控制器，就是一个在自己的 ``cam:`` 小节中声明文件类型的包（参见 :ref:`cam-section` "
"），可以由上面那个选项来指定，也可以由对象自己的 ``implementation:`` 指定，或者用 ``-i`` 为单次运行指定。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:88
msgid ""
"Every key of the object's section is also a parameter of that file type, "
"which makes the two of them three layers of one namespace: the built-in "
"package underneath, the package's own ``cam:`` section, then the object's "
"``manufacturing:``. A package cutting twenty parts from one sheet sets the "
"tool once; the one part that needs a smaller cutter says so for itself. "
"Lengths, feeds and speeds may each carry a unit and are converted at every "
"layer, so a ``mm/min`` written by the package is understood as surely as one"
" written on the object."
msgstr ""
"对象小节中的每一个键同时也是该文件类型的一个参数，于是两者构成了同一个命名空间的三层：最底下是内置包，然后是包自己的 ``cam:`` "
"小节，再然后是对象的 ``manufacturing:`` "
"。一个要从同一张板材上切出二十个零件的包只需设置一次刀具；唯独那个需要更小刀具的零件自己说明一下即可。长度、进给和转速都可以各自带上单位，并在每一层都会做换算，因此包里写的"
" ``mm/min`` 和写在对象上的一样能被准确理解。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:97
msgid ""
"What comes back is a file beside the package -- ``panel.nc`` -- and what it "
"counted: how many passes, how deep, how far the tool travels in the cut. The"
" route is the object's outline **sectioned at the bottom of the cut**, "
"offset by the radius of the cutter, and that is both what makes it right for"
" a prismatic object and the limit worth knowing about every other one: where"
" the cross-section changes over the cut, no single outline is right, and the"
" route follows the bottom and says so as a warning naming how much the two "
"ends differ by. A route produced from an outline nobody expected is the one "
"failure that looks like a success all the way to the machine."
msgstr ""
"返回的是一个放在包旁边的文件—— ``panel.nc`` ——以及它统计出来的数据：走了多少刀、每刀多深、刀具在切削中走了多远。刀路是对象轮廓 "
"**在切削底面处的剖面** "
"，再按刀具半径做偏置，这既是它对棱柱形对象正确的原因，也是对其他所有对象都值得了解的局限：当横截面在切削深度范围内发生变化时，没有任何单一轮廓是正确的，刀路会沿着底面走，并以一条警告说明两端相差多少。由一条谁也没料到的轮廓生成的刀路，是那种一路到了机床跟前都还看着像成功的失败。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:107
msgid ""
"``pc test`` runs the same thing as its ``cam`` check -- it produces the "
"route and passes the object only if one came back -- and applies it to an "
"object that declares the section and to nothing else, so a package of bolts "
"pays nothing for it. Unlike the analyses it does not keep what it produced: "
"a route a check wrote would be indistinguishable from the one ``pc cam`` "
"writes, so it routes into a temporary directory and deletes it."
msgstr ""
"``pc test`` 的 ``cam`` "
"检查运行的正是同一套流程——生成刀路，只有确实生成出来了才让该对象通过——并且只作用于声明了该小节的对象，别的一概不管，因此一个装满螺栓的包不会为此付出任何代价。与各项分析不同，它不会保留生成的结果：检查写出的刀路与"
" ``pc cam`` 写出的无从分辨，所以它把刀路生成到一个临时目录里，然后删掉。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:114
msgid ""
"The check that used to be called ``cam`` is ``manufacturability``. It asks "
"whether an object can be made or bought *at all* -- whether its geometry "
"suits the method it declares, whether what it is made from is reproducible, "
"whether a supplier could be found -- which is a different question from "
"whether a post-processor can produce a program for it. One word answered "
"both until ``pc cam`` existed. ``-f`` filters by name prefix, so ``-f "
"manufacturability`` selects that check and its seven method-specific "
"siblings and ``-f cam`` selects the route check alone."
msgstr ""
"过去叫做 ``cam`` 的那项检查现在叫 ``manufacturability`` 。它问的是某个对象 *究竟* 能不能被制造或采购 -- "
"它的几何是否适合它所声明的那种方式、它所用的东西是否可复现、是否找得到供应商 -- 而这与“某个后处理器能不能为它生成一个程序”是不同的问题。在 "
"``pc cam`` 出现之前，一个词同时回答了这两个问题。``-f`` 是按名称前缀过滤的，所以 ``-f manufacturability`` "
"会选中该检查及其七个针对具体工艺方法的同族检查，而 ``-f cam`` 只会选中加工路径这一项检查。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build.rst:123
msgid ""
"`examples/feature_cam "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad/tree/main/examples/feature_cam>`_ is the"
" three operations on three objects, and a fourth that declares no section "
"and is passed over. See :ref:`pc cam <cam>` for the command and the units it"
" accepts."
msgstr ""
"`examples/feature_cam "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad/tree/main/examples/feature_cam>`_ "
"就是三个对象上的三道工序，再加上第四个什么小节都不声明、因而被跳过的对象。该命令以及它所接受的各种单位参见 :ref:`pc cam <cam>` 。"

